## Objective

Build the Clock-In Addresses management page. This is where Owners and Admins manage geofence locations that employees must be within to clock in (when the clock-in mode is set to "Specific Addresses" or "Active Job Sites"). Addresses can be created manually, imported from a quote's jobsite address, or imported from a lead's address.

**Page:** Implemented as an "Addresses" tab within the Settings page at `/settings/time-clock/page.tsx` (per the contract's Section 7.9 which lists Addresses as a settings tab). Extract to a component file for maintainability: `app/src/components/time-clock/ClockinAddressesTab.tsx`.

**Roles:** Owner, Admin only

---

## Task 1 — Test All 7 Endpoints

```bash
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/login \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"email":"ludsonaiello@gmail.com","password":"978@F32c"}' | jq -r .access_token)

# 1. List addresses (with filters)
curl -s -X GET "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/addresses?page=1&limit=20" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | jq .

# 2. List with active filter
curl -s -X GET "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/addresses?is_active=true" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | jq .

# 3. Create address manually
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/addresses \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "label": "Test Office",
    "address_line1": "123 Main St",
    "city": "Boston",
    "state": "MA",
    "zip_code": "02101",
    "radius_meters": 100
  }' | jq .

# 4. Get single address (replace ID from create response)
# curl -s -X GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/addresses/{ID} \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | jq .

# 5. Update address (replace ID)
# curl -s -X PATCH http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/addresses/{ID} \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"label": "Updated Office", "radius_meters": 150}' | jq .

# 6. Delete (soft-delete, replace ID)
# curl -s -X DELETE http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/addresses/{ID} \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | jq .

# 7. Test import-from-quote (need a valid quote_id)
# First, list quotes to get an ID:
curl -s -X GET "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/quotes?limit=5" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | jq '.data[0].id'

# curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/addresses/import-from-quote \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"quote_id":"QUOTE_ID","label":"Quote Site"}' | jq .

# 8. Test import-from-lead (need a valid lead_address_id)
# First, list leads to get address IDs:
curl -s -X GET "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/leads?limit=5" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | jq '.data[0]'

# curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/addresses/import-from-lead \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"lead_address_id":"LEAD_ADDRESS_ID","label":"Lead Site"}' | jq .
```

Record all response shapes. Pay special attention to:
- Whether the list response includes `project` relation data (project name)
- How `source` field is returned (enum value)
- Whether lat/lng are returned as numbers or strings
- The create response shape (does it return the geocoded lat/lng?)

