## Task 8 — Project Dropdown (Shared)

The project dropdown is used in multiple places (create address, edit address, import tabs). Create a shared hook or component:

```typescript
// Hook approach
const useProjects = () => {
  const [projects, setProjects] = useState<Array<{ id: string; name: string }>>([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);

  const loadProjects = async () => {
    setLoading(true);
    try {
      // Use existing project list endpoint
      const response = await apiClient.get('/projects', { params: { status: 'in_progress', limit: 200 } });
      setProjects(response.data.data || response.data);
    } catch {
      toast.error('Failed to load projects');
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  };

  return { projects, loading, loadProjects };
};
```

Find the existing projects API and endpoint to ensure correct field names (`name` vs `title`, etc.). The project model uses `name` (not `title`).

