## Task 9 — Radius Visual Helper

Add a small visual helper below the radius input to give context:

```
Radius: [100] meters
≈ 328 feet | About the size of a football field
```

Conversion: 1 meter = 3.281 feet. Show a contextual size comparison:
- 25m: "About 80 feet — small building"
- 50m: "About 164 feet — half a city block"
- 100m: "About 328 feet — a football field"
- 200m: "About 656 feet — two city blocks"
- 500m: "About 1640 feet — a quarter mile"
- 1000m+: "About {feet} feet — {miles} miles"

This helps non-technical admins understand what the radius means in practical terms.

